# Local verification

Agent shells often set `NODE_ENV=production`, so a bare `npm install` omits `vitest` and `tsx`. That is not a missing `node_modules` tree. Never tell the user tests were skipped because `node_modules` is missing.

If `node_modules/.bin/vitest` is absent, run `NODE_ENV=development npm install --include=dev`.

This workspace path contains colons. Do not put `$PWD/node_modules/.bin` on `PATH` (colons split PATH). Invoke binaries with a quoted path:

```bash
NODE_ENV=test "./node_modules/.bin/vitest" run
```

Run the Vitest (and Playwright, when UI/e2e changed) for the slice you touched. CI remains the merge gate; it does not replace local runs when the bins exist.
